{"type":"system","subtype":"task_notification","task_id":"bvq6rr4d7","tool_use_id":"toolu_01Nhhmfz6DNk9kUa9b73QF1M","status":"completed","output_file":"/tmp/claude-441489/-scratch-users-kushinm-auto-psych-outer-loop-live-runs-run3-repo/fbe46fa4-102a-48d3-81a6-ec3c33bd929b/tasks/bvq6rr4d7.output","summary":"Background command \"D=/scratch/users/kushinm/auto-psych/outer_loop_live/run3/data/subjective_randomness/experiment2/model_loop/iter_1/candidate_5\ncat << 'EOF' > $D/model_name.txt\nswitch_belief_habitual_side_lapse\nEOF\ncat << 'EOF' > $D/hypothesis.md\nRefinement of `personal_chance_switch_belief`: people still judge a sequence random to the extent their own model of a fair coin (with a person-specific belief about how often chance switches) explains it better than the regular generators (a switch-biased Markov coin, a biased coin, and a repeating short motif with occasional slips), with the evidence weighed per flip and person-specific decisiveness. The single change is that on a person-specific fraction of trials people do not make the judgment at all and simply click their own habitual side (each person has their own default side preference), so every person's choices are pulled towards their preferred button by a fixed share even on clear-cut pairs — addressing the critique that participants' individual rates of choosing Left vary more than a model without response habits produces.\nEOF\npython - << 'PY'\nsrc=open('/scratch/users/kushinm/auto-psych/outer_loop_live/run3/data/subjective_randomness/experiment2/model_loop/models/personal_chance_switch_belief.py').read()\nhead='''\"\"\"Person-specific chance switch belief plus habitual-side lapses.\n\nRefinement of `personal_chance_switch_belief`: a sequence looks random to the\nextent the person's model of a fair coin (switching with person-specific\nprobability q) explains it better than the regular generators (Markov coin,\nbiased coin, repeating motif with slips; unknowns integrated out), the log\nevidence weighed per flip by a fitted power of length, with person-specific\ndecision sensitivity. Single change: on a person-specific fraction lambda_i of\ntrials the person skips the judgment and clicks their own habitual side\n(Left with person-specific probability pi_i), so\np_left = (1 - lambda_i) * p_judge + lambda_i * pi_i.\n\"\"\"\n'''\nbody=src[src.index('import math'):]\nold='''    p_left = pm.Deterministic(\n        \"p_left\", pm.math.sigmoid(beta[participant_id] * score_diff)\n    )\n'''\nnew='''    p_judge = pm.math.sigmoid(beta[participant_id] * score_diff)\n\n    # Person-specific habitual-side lapses: rate lambda_i of skipping the\n    # judgment, and the side pi_i (probability of Left) clicked when they do.\n    mu_logit_lam = pm.Normal(\"mu_logit_lam\", mu=-2.5, sigma=1.0)\n    sigma_logit_lam = pm.HalfNormal(\"sigma_logit_lam\", sigma=0.75)\n    z_lam = pm.Normal(\"z_lam\", mu=0.0, sigma=1.0, shape=400)\n    lam = pm.math.sigmoid(mu_logit_lam + sigma_logit_lam * z_lam)\n    mu_logit_pi = pm.Normal(\"mu_logit_pi\", mu=0.0, sigma=1.0)\n    sigma_logit_pi = pm.HalfNormal(\"sigma_logit_pi\", sigma=1.0)\n    z_pi = pm.Normal(\"z_pi\", mu=0.0, sigma=1.0, shape=400)\n    pi_side = pm.math.sigmoid(mu_logit_pi + sigma_logit_pi * z_pi)\n\n    lam_i = lam[participant_id]\n    p_left = pm.Deterministic(\n        \"p_left\",\n        pt.clip((1.0 - lam_i) * p_judge + lam_i * pi_side[participant_id], 1e-6, 1 - 1e-6),\n    )\n'''\nassert old in body\nopen('$D/candidate.py'.replace('$D','/scratch/users/kushinm/auto-psych/outer_loop_live/run3/data/subjective_randomness/experiment2/model_loop/iter_1/candidate_5'),'w').write(head+'\\n'+body.replace(old,new))\nPY\ncd /scratch/users/kushinm/auto-psych/outer_loop_live/runs/run3/repo && /scratch/users/kushinm/auto-psych/outer_loop_live/venv/bin/python -m src.pipelines.inner_loop.check_candidate --candidate-dir $D --responses /scratch/users/kushinm/auto-psych/outer_loop_live/run3/data/subjective_randomness/experiment2/model_loop/responses.csv 2>&1 | tail -5\" completed (exit code 0)","uuid":"d94738a8-c4fd-4d2d-a6fa-9c92f534ffb7","session_id":"fbe46fa4-102a-48d3-81a6-ec3c33bd929b"}
