{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CfiX1Ej2UXPMcAbUXesyH","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Candidate 5 is written and passes the self-check (`OK`). The smoke fit's ELPD-LOO is −2108.2, about the same as the incumbent's −2107.3. That number comes from a short single-chain run, so it is only a rough guide.\n\n**What I refined:** `personal_chance_switch_belief`, the rank-1 model, which is statistically tied with the incumbent. The new model is named `switch_belief_habitual_side_lapse`.\n\n**The one change:** on some share of trials, which differs by person, a participant skips the randomness judgment and clicks their usual side. Each person also has their own preferred side. So:\n\np_left = (1 − λᵢ)·p_judge + λᵢ·πᵢ\n\nwhere λᵢ is how often person *i* skips the judgment and πᵢ is how often they pick Left when they do. Both come from population distributions with 400 slots each, so the next design can predict new participants.\n\nThis targets the critique's one finding: people's individual rates of choosing Left vary more than the incumbent produces (p = 0.014, though it doesn't survive the FDR correction, q = 0.112). It is also a different mechanism from the side-bias model that already lost (`person_side_bias_chance_vs_motif`, 210 nats behind). That one adds a bias inside the judgment, so it barely matters when the evidence is strong. Here the habitual clicks pull choices towards a person's side even on clear-cut pairs, and they cap how decisive anyone can be.\n\n**Risks at admission:**\n- **Convergence:** the self-check doesn't test it. A person's side preference is only weakly pinned down when that person rarely skips the judgment, which can make sampling hard. That could fail the convergence gate or the 30-minute fit limit.\n- **Unreliable PSIS-LOO:** 6.9% of trials had high Pareto-k on the smoke fit, against a 1% tolerance. If that persists in the full fit, admission will treat the model's ELPD-LOO as untrustworthy.\n\nFiles are in `experiment2/model_loop/iter_1/candidate_5/`:\n- `hypothesis.md`\n- `model_name.txt`\n- `candidate.py`"}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2595,"cache_read_input_tokens":72327,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":2595,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":2,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"fbe46fa4-102a-48d3-81a6-ec3c33bd929b","uuid":"214229d6-512b-4c39-ac9f-8bf62fe8f331","timestamp":"2026-10-05T05:13:23.045Z","request_id":"req_011CfiX1EGk5CDnTDKZ3h16D"}
